{"id": "EUVD-2026-103588", "enisaUuid": "943334f8-c558-357e-b0ca-f698420f5810", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: fs/xattr: don't assume the inode is locked in path_unlink/path_rmdir\n\nbpf_lsm_has_d_inode_locked() makes the verifier rewrite\nbpf_[set|remove]_dentry_xattr() to the _locked variants, which assume\nthat the caller already holds the inode's i_rwsem.  The path_unlink and\npath_rmdir hooks are listed, but security_path_unlink() and\nsecurity_path_rmdir() run before vfs_unlink()/vfs_rmdir() take the\nvictim inode's i_rwsem, so a sleepable BPF LSM program attached to\neither hook mutates the victim's xattrs without the lock held.\n\nDrop the two path hooks from d_inode_locked_hooks so that the verifier\nkeeps the locking bpf_[set|remove]_dentry_xattr() variants, which take\nthe lock themselves.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:18:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:21:26", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7504b677c4370c9e4b153c553ff8831c093b1ff6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/640d37fbd34d03af727dbc567f48c0203d1de6b4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/35d442ed1f86465e49df3119fb898f985186db13"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98543", "GHSA-mhp5-jj6j-c7m7"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "37d51901-9af5-386e-b336-978345aaeadb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "56467292794b800164df20c076c409ac548e56ec <35d442ed1f86465e49df3119fb898f985186db13"}, {"id": "570fc912-888c-39d4-aedb-61af16d42fe1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15"}, {"id": "77e538ce-1f3a-3ecf-a3be-d4198ef63868", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "56467292794b800164df20c076c409ac548e56ec <640d37fbd34d03af727dbc567f48c0203d1de6b4"}, {"id": "7b1416fe-e798-356b-8dd4-a33896345ee5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "56467292794b800164df20c076c409ac548e56ec <7504b677c4370c9e4b153c553ff8831c093b1ff6"}, {"id": "7f7f2f5b-71bb-374c-8efa-49f4e50ed28b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "bd8a9e04-e8c7-37c3-b27d-5281d694346d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "c78d63f0-82ca-3a4c-b6c4-0a24f1158b48", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "f45595c7-f9cb-362f-9e23-b6a913073f4a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7b5b8c26-4e57-3544-83a0-5bd6bbf6bbfb", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}